      "//": "2-WAY GATE (glmm vs lme4), no jl_formula, by decision rather than by MixedModels limitation: this rung's job is the sparse arm's se_hessian at large theta-hat, and lme4 is the comparator that quantity is calibrated against. MixedModels.jl also throws PosDefException on rung 45, the dense large-theta rung, so a Julia leg in the same theta-hat band would most likely just crash. Same convention as rungs 23/24 and 36: absent jl_formula means engines/mixedmodels.jl skips the rung. Seven crossed intercept-only extras is what routes this to the sparse solver (over MAX_EXTRA_GROUPINGS); every RE block is scalar on purpose, because engines/lme4.R emits stddev_se only for all-scalar binomial/poisson fits and stddev_se is half of what this rung gates. Bernoulli, not Poisson: a Poisson design in this regime pushes counts into the tens of thousands, where the deviance-sum rounding noise dominates the FD Hessian's step independent of any solver tuning (see prep/gen_large_theta_data.R block R4 for the measurement); a Bernoulli response bounds the working weight and removes that noise floor. Sparse-large-theta-hat Poisson coverage is deliberately not attempted for this reason, not a gap left open."
